\[x^2 = 6-5x^2 + y^2.\]From the right triangle $XAO,$ $XO = x$ and $AO = r,$ so $XA = \sqrt{x^2 + r^2}.$  From the right triangle $PAX,$ $PA = 2r$ and $PX = \sqrt{x^2 + (y-r)^2}.$  Then by the Pythagorean Theorem applied to $\triangle PAX$,
\[PA^2 = PX^2 + AX^2,\]so
\[4r^2 = x^2 + (y-r)^2 + x^2 + r^2.\]This simplifies to $r^2 = y^2 - 2yr.$  From the right triangle $YAO,$ $YO = 3r$ and $AO = r,$ so $YA = 3r.$  From the right triangle $PAO,$ $PA = 2r$ and $PO = x + r,$ so
\[PO^2 = PA^2 + AO^2,\]so
\[(x + r)^2 = (3r)^2 + x^2 + r^2 = 10r^2 + x^2.\]Then
\begin{align*}
10r^2 + x^2 &= (r + x)^2 \\
&= x^2 + 2rx + r^2 \\
&= r(2x + r).
\end{align*}Substituting $r^2$ for $y^2 - 2yz,$ we get
\[r(2x + r) = r(y^2 - 2yr + r) = r(y-r)(y+r),\]so $x = r.$  But we know that $x^2 = 6 - 5x^2 + y^2 - 4r^2 = 6 - 5x^2 + r^2,$ so $x = \pm 1.$  Then $r = x = 1.$

